{
  "_comment": "Theme registry for chromaticli. Each `.themes.<id>` maps a chromaticli internal id to a VSCode theme (display name + extension) and a 16-color terminal palette. Palette values should match the upstream theme's canonical iTerm2 port — never hand-tune; the goal is fidelity to the editor experience. Palettes are emitted via standard OSC codes (OSC 4/10/11/12) so they apply uniformly across iTerm2, Terminal.app, Alacritty, Kitty, and any modern terminal. Editing workflow: after any change under `.themes` or `.pairs`, run (1) `python3 scripts/verify-themes.py` to confirm every `vscode.theme_id` resolves against the live VSCode marketplace or matches a known built-in, then (2) `python3 scripts/generate-preview.py` to refresh `docs/themes/*.svg`, `docs/theme_preview.html`, and `docs/theme_preview.md`. Commit themes.json and the regenerated artifacts together. CI runs both as separate jobs.",
